window.REV_FLIP=window.REV_FLIP||{};window.REV_FLIP["autogen"]=[{"id":"autogen-f0001","card":"q-autogen-001-overview","sec":"autogen-s001","q":"Which Python package provides AutoGen, and how do you import it?","a":"<p>The package is <code>pyautogen</code>. You import it as <code>import autogen</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0002","card":"q-autogen-001-overview","sec":"autogen-s001","q":"Who teaches the course on building AI agents with AutoGen, and what is it called?","a":"<p>The course is <em>Building AI Agents with AutoGen</em> by Harshit Tyagi.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0003","card":"q-autogen-002-1-core-concepts-interview-essentials","sec":"autogen-s002","q":"What is an AI agent made of?","a":"<p>An AI agent is an LLM plus tools plus memory plus context. Its components are an LLM for language understanding, document access, a toolkit (APIs, calculators), conversation ability, and a database for memory.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0004","card":"q-autogen-002-1-core-concepts-interview-essentials","sec":"autogen-s002","q":"What is AutoGen?","a":"<p>A multi-agent conversational framework from Microsoft. Agents have different roles and solve tasks with different tools and patterns.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0005","card":"q-autogen-002-1-core-concepts-interview-essentials","sec":"autogen-s002","q":"What can an AutoGen agent do, and what can power it?","a":"<p>An agent can send messages, receive messages and generate replies. It can be powered by an LLM, a code executor (for example an IPython kernel), human input, or a combination.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0006","card":"q-autogen-002-1-core-concepts-interview-essentials","sec":"autogen-s002","q":"Why use several agents instead of one big LLM?","a":"<p>Five reasons:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Specialization: each agent does one thing well.</li>\n  <li>Collaboration: multiple perspectives give better quality.</li>\n  <li>Scalability: you can add agents.</li>\n  <li>Flexibility: custom roles.</li>\n  <li>Efficiency: parallel work.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0007","card":"q-autogen-002-1-core-concepts-interview-essentials","sec":"autogen-s002","q":"How do AI agents compare with human assistants, and how should you frame them?","a":"<p>Agents are available 24/7, do not tire, are consistent, handle many tasks at once and learn continuously. Frame them as collaborators that augment people, not replacements.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0008","card":"q-autogen-002-1-core-concepts-interview-essentials","sec":"autogen-s002","q":"Which design patterns does the AutoGen course teach?","a":"<p><strong>Reflection</strong> (self or peer review), <strong>Tool Use</strong> (functions and APIs) and <strong>Multi-Agent Collaboration</strong> (sequential chats, nested chats, group chat). It also covers human-in-the-loop and agent memory (teachability).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0009","card":"q-autogen-003-1-core-concepts-interview-essentials","sec":"autogen-s002","q":"What conversation shapes and collaboration shapes exist in multi-agent systems?","a":"<p>Conversation shapes are two-way (agent to agent), multi-way (group) and nested (hierarchical). Collaboration shapes are sequential, parallel and hierarchical (manager-worker).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0010","card":"q-autogen-003-1-core-concepts-interview-essentials","sec":"autogen-s002","q":"What is the problem-solving approach for a multi-agent team?","a":"<p>Break a complex problem into subtasks, assign them to specialized agents, let them collaborate, then synthesize the result. For example, a Researcher gathers, an Analyst analyzes and a Writer reports.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0011","card":"q-autogen-003-1-core-concepts-interview-essentials","sec":"autogen-s002","q":"Which example teams does the AutoGen course mention?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Software: architect, developer, tester, documenter.</li>\n  <li>Content: researcher, outliner, writer, editor.</li>\n  <li>Business intelligence: collector, analyst, visualizer, reporter.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0012","card":"q-autogen-003-1-core-concepts-interview-essentials","sec":"autogen-s002","q":"What is the order of topics in the AutoGen course?","a":"<p>Multi-agent conversations, research assistant (sequential chats), nested chats, tool use and internet, coding copilot, teachable agents, then the group chat company.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0013","card":"q-autogen-003-1-core-concepts-interview-essentials","sec":"autogen-s002","q":"In the AutoGen intro, how is the Researcher, Analyst and Writer team sketched in code?","a":"<p>It is conceptual pseudo-code, not a real AutoGen API. Each role passes its result to the next:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>researcher = Agent(&quot;Gather data on topic&quot;)\nanalyst = Agent(&quot;Analyze findings&quot;)\nwriter = Agent(&quot;Create report&quot;)\n\ndata = researcher.research()\ninsights = analyst.analyze(data)\nreport = writer.write(insights)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0014","card":"q-autogen-004-2-setup-and-conversableagent","sec":"autogen-s003","q":"What is <code>ConversableAgent</code> in AutoGen?","a":"<p>The built-in generic agent class. Different roles use the same interface.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0015","card":"q-autogen-004-2-setup-and-conversableagent","sec":"autogen-s003","q":"Which four components does <code>ConversableAgent</code> bundle?","a":"<p><strong>LLM configuration</strong>, <strong>code executor</strong>, <strong>function/tool executor</strong> and <strong>human-in-the-loop</strong>. They are switchable and customizable.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0016","card":"q-autogen-004-2-setup-and-conversableagent","sec":"autogen-s003","q":"How do you install AutoGen, and what goes in the course project's <code>requirements.txt</code>?","a":"<p>Install with:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>pip install pyautogen</code></pre></div>\n<p><code>requirements.txt</code> lists <code>pyautogen</code> and <code>python-dotenv</code>. The <code>.env</code> file holds the key and is gitignored.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0017","card":"q-autogen-005-environment-variables-and-llm-config","sec":"autogen-s004","q":"How should you handle API keys in an AutoGen project?","a":"<p>Never hard-code them. Store them in <code>.env</code> (for example <code>OPENAI_API_KEY=your_api_key_here</code>) and load them with <code>python-dotenv</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0018","card":"q-autogen-005-environment-variables-and-llm-config","sec":"autogen-s004","q":"What does <code>load_dotenv()</code> return?","a":"<p>It returns <code>True</code> when the <code>.env</code> file was found.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0019","card":"q-autogen-005-environment-variables-and-llm-config","sec":"autogen-s004","q":"How do you define a single LLM config in AutoGen?","a":"<p>Use a dict with the model and the key from the environment:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>llm_config = {\n    &quot;model&quot;: &quot;gpt-4o&quot;,\n    &quot;api_key&quot;: os.getenv(&quot;OPENAI_API_KEY&quot;)\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0020","card":"q-autogen-005-environment-variables-and-llm-config","sec":"autogen-s004","q":"How do you configure several LLMs in AutoGen, and why would you?","a":"<p>Use a <code>config_list</code> of dicts. Reasons are fallback, cost optimisation, and mixing cloud with local models.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>config_list = [\n    {&quot;model&quot;: &quot;gpt-4o&quot;, &quot;api_key&quot;: os.getenv(&quot;OPENAI_API_KEY&quot;)},\n    {&quot;model&quot;: &quot;llama-7b&quot;, &quot;base_url&quot;: &quot;http://localhost:8080&quot;}  # local server\n]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0021","card":"q-autogen-005-environment-variables-and-llm-config","sec":"autogen-s004","q":"How do you configure a local LLM only in AutoGen, and why?","a":"<p>Point <code>base_url</code> at the local server. The benefits are privacy and no API cost.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>llm_config = {\n    &quot;model&quot;: &quot;llama-7b&quot;,\n    &quot;base_url&quot;: &quot;http://localhost:8080&quot;\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0022","card":"q-autogen-005-environment-variables-and-llm-config","sec":"autogen-s004","q":"In AutoGen, how do you check in code that the environment was loaded?","a":"<p>Test the return value of <code>load_dotenv()</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if load_dotenv():\n    print(&quot;Environment variables loaded&quot;)\nelse:\n    print(&quot;Error loading .env file&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0023","card":"q-autogen-006-minimal-chatbot","sec":"autogen-s005","q":"How do you create a minimal chatbot agent with <code>ConversableAgent</code>?","a":"<p>Pass a name, the LLM config and <code>human_input_mode=\"NEVER\"</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>agent = ConversableAgent(\n    name=&quot;chatbot&quot;,\n    llm_config=llm_config,\n    human_input_mode=&quot;NEVER&quot;\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0024","card":"q-autogen-006-minimal-chatbot","sec":"autogen-s005","q":"How do you send a message to an agent and get a reply with <code>generate_reply</code>?","a":"<p>Pass a list of message dicts. Each has <code>content</code> (your query) and <code>role</code> (<code>\"user\"</code>). <code>generate_reply(messages=...)</code> returns the LLM's response.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>messages = [\n    {\n        &quot;content&quot;: &quot;How to make delicious ramen?&quot;,\n        &quot;role&quot;: &quot;user&quot;\n    }\n]\nreply = agent.generate_reply(messages=messages)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0025","card":"q-autogen-006-minimal-chatbot","sec":"autogen-s005","q":"What do the <code>name</code> and <code>llm_config</code> parameters of <code>ConversableAgent</code> do?","a":"<p><code>name</code> is the agent identifier. Use descriptive names such as <code>marketing_assistant</code>, not <code>agent1</code>. <code>llm_config</code> is a dict (single LLM) or a config list. It lets agents converse in natural language, convert between structured and unstructured text, and understand context.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0026","card":"q-autogen-006-minimal-chatbot","sec":"autogen-s005","q":"How do you make a researcher and a writer agent with the same interface?","a":"<p>Create two <code>ConversableAgent</code> objects that differ only in name (and the question you ask):</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>researcher = ConversableAgent(name=&quot;researcher&quot;, llm_config=llm_config, human_input_mode=&quot;NEVER&quot;)\nwriter = ConversableAgent(name=&quot;writer&quot;, llm_config=llm_config, human_input_mode=&quot;NEVER&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0027","card":"q-autogen-007-debugging-a-broken-setup","sec":"autogen-s006","q":"What are the causes and fixes for common AutoGen setup errors?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Cause</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>API key error</td><td>Missing/invalid key</td><td>Check <code>.env</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Import error</td><td>AutoGen not installed</td><td><code>pip install pyautogen</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>load_dotenv()</code> returns <code>False</code></td><td><code>.env</code> missing</td><td>Create <code>.env</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>No response</td><td>Wrong model name</td><td>Verify model name</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0028","card":"q-autogen-007-debugging-a-broken-setup","sec":"autogen-s006","q":"Why would an AutoGen agent give no response?","a":"<p>The model name is probably wrong. Verify the model name.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0029","card":"q-autogen-007-debugging-a-broken-setup","sec":"autogen-s006","q":"Which checks confirm an AutoGen setup works?","a":"<p>Print these and check the results:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>print(load_dotenv())                  # Should be True\nprint(os.getenv(&quot;OPENAI_API_KEY&quot;))    # Should not be None\nprint(llm_config)                     # Shows model and api_key\nprint(agent.name)                     # Confirms agent creation</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0030","card":"q-autogen-008-3-agent-types-and-human-input-modes","sec":"autogen-s007","q":"What are the three AutoGen agent classes and what is each used for?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Agent class</th><th>Primary use</th><th>Key feature</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>ConversableAgent</code></td><td>General purpose</td><td>Flexible configuration; base class</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>AssistantAgent</code></td><td>LLM assistant, code generation</td><td>Pre-set system message for coding/language tasks; usually <code>code_execution_config=False</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>UserProxyAgent</code></td><td>Represents the human</td><td>Human input integration, optional code execution</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0031","card":"q-autogen-008-3-agent-types-and-human-input-modes","sec":"autogen-s007","q":"What does <code>UserProxyAgent</code> represent in AutoGen?","a":"<p>The human. It integrates human input and can optionally execute code.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0032","card":"q-autogen-008-3-agent-types-and-human-input-modes","sec":"autogen-s007","q":"What does <code>AssistantAgent</code> have that the base class does not?","a":"<p>A pre-set system message for coding and language tasks. It is usually used with <code>code_execution_config=False</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0033","card":"q-autogen-008-3-agent-types-and-human-input-modes","sec":"autogen-s007","q":"What does <code>human_input_mode=\"NEVER\"</code> do?","a":"<p>The agent is fully automated. The human never interrupts.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0034","card":"q-autogen-008-3-agent-types-and-human-input-modes","sec":"autogen-s007","q":"What does <code>human_input_mode=\"ALWAYS\"</code> do, and when do you use it?","a":"<p>The human is asked for input at every turn. It is used for oversight of code execution or web search.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0035","card":"q-autogen-008-3-agent-types-and-human-input-modes","sec":"autogen-s007","q":"What does <code>human_input_mode=\"TERMINATE\"</code> do?","a":"<p>The human is asked only when the conversation is about to end.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0036","card":"q-autogen-009-4-conversation-termination","sec":"autogen-s008","q":"How does <code>is_termination_msg</code> work in AutoGen?","a":"<p>It takes a function over the message dict. Returning <code>True</code> ends the chat.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0037","card":"q-autogen-009-4-conversation-termination","sec":"autogen-s008","q":"How do you end a chat when a message contains \"exit\"?","a":"<p>Pass a lambda as <code>is_termination_msg</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>is_termination_msg=lambda msg: &quot;exit&quot; in msg.get(&quot;content&quot;, &quot;&quot;).lower()</code></pre></div>\n<p>If the tutor replies with \"exit\", the condition fires and there is no second turn.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0038","card":"q-autogen-009-4-conversation-termination","sec":"autogen-s008","q":"How do you write a custom termination function that ends the chat on several keywords?","a":"<p>Check whether any keyword appears in the lowercased content:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def custom_termination(msg):\n    content = msg.get(&quot;content&quot;, &quot;&quot;).lower()\n    return any(word in content for word in [&quot;done&quot;, &quot;complete&quot;, &quot;finished&quot;])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0039","card":"q-autogen-009-4-conversation-termination","sec":"autogen-s008","q":"Which other loop guards exist in AutoGen besides <code>is_termination_msg</code>?","a":"<p><code>max_turns</code> (per chat), <code>max_round</code> (group chat), and timeouts on code executors.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0040","card":"q-autogen-010-5-sequential-chats-research-assistant","sec":"autogen-s009","q":"What is the project and which roles make up the sequential-chat research assistant?","a":"<p>A marketing-video research assistant. The roles are:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Manager</strong> (<code>UserProxyAgent</code>): supplies the topic, selects ideas, decides.</li>\n  <li><strong>Idea Generator</strong>: several campaign concepts.</li>\n  <li><strong>Script Writer</strong>: full script with dialog, scenes and camera directions.</li>\n  <li><strong>Script Reviewer</strong>: coherence, engagement and alignment with the topic.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0041","card":"q-autogen-010-5-sequential-chats-research-assistant","sec":"autogen-s009","q":"In the AutoGen sequential-chat research assistant, what is the flow of the marketing research assistant?","a":"<p>Manager to Idea Generator, then Manager picks or refines an idea, then Script Writer, then Script Reviewer, then the Manager makes the final decision.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0042","card":"q-autogen-010-5-sequential-chats-research-assistant","sec":"autogen-s009","q":"What are the three phases of building a sequential-chat workflow?","a":"<p>Create agents (roles), define tasks (a list of chat dicts), then initiate chats with <code>initiate_chats</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0043","card":"q-autogen-010-5-sequential-chats-research-assistant","sec":"autogen-s009","q":"What do the keys of a chat dict mean in sequential chats?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Key</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>sender</code> / <code>recipient</code></td><td>Who initiates / who receives</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>message</code></td><td>Task instruction (string, or a function in nested chats)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>summary_method</code></td><td><code>\"reflection_with_llm\"</code> = LLM writes the summary (smarter, uses context); <code>\"last_msg\"</code> = last message as summary (faster, less context)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>summary_args</code></td><td>e.g. <code>{\"summary_prompt\": \"...\"}</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>max_turns</code></td><td>Conversation limit: <code>2+</code> allows iterative refinement, <code>1</code> is a single response</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>clear_history</code></td><td><code>True</code> = independent task starts fresh; <code>False</code> = carries context from previous chats</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0044","card":"q-autogen-010-5-sequential-chats-research-assistant","sec":"autogen-s009","q":"When do sequential chats fit best?","a":"<p>When each task depends on the previous result. The summary of one chat is carried into the next.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0045","card":"q-autogen-010-5-sequential-chats-research-assistant","sec":"autogen-s009","q":"What is the difference between <code>summary_method</code> values <code>\"reflection_with_llm\"</code> and <code>\"last_msg\"</code>?","a":"<p><code>\"reflection_with_llm\"</code> lets an LLM write the summary, which is smarter and uses context. <code>\"last_msg\"</code> uses the last message as the summary, which is faster but has less context.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0046","card":"q-autogen-010-5-sequential-chats-research-assistant","sec":"autogen-s009","q":"What do <code>max_turns</code> and <code>clear_history</code> control in a chat dict?","a":"<p><code>max_turns</code> limits the conversation: 2 or more allows iterative refinement, 1 is a single response. <code>clear_history</code> set to <code>True</code> starts an independent task fresh. <code>False</code> carries context from previous chats.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0047","card":"q-autogen-010-5-sequential-chats-research-assistant","sec":"autogen-s009","q":"What is the prompt-quality rule for agent system messages and task messages?","a":"<p>Detailed, specific messages beat vague ones. For example, \"Generate 3-5 innovative campaign ideas for eco-friendly home cleaning products. Include potential storylines.\" is better than \"Give me ideas\".</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0048","card":"q-autogen-011-agents","sec":"autogen-s010","q":"Why does the Manager in the research assistant use <code>UserProxyAgent</code> with <code>code_execution_config=False</code>?","a":"<p><code>UserProxyAgent</code> represents the human's interests. There is no code to run, so code execution is switched off.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>manager_proxy = UserProxyAgent(\n    name=&quot;manager_proxy&quot;,\n    human_input_mode=&quot;NEVER&quot;,\n    code_execution_config=False,\n    llm_config=llm_config\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0049","card":"q-autogen-011-agents","sec":"autogen-s010","q":"What is the Manager agent's role in its system message?","a":"<p>A marketing campaign manager. It provides campaign topics, evaluates ideas and scripts from the creative team, and makes final decisions on campaign direction.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0050","card":"q-autogen-011-agents","sec":"autogen-s010","q":"What responsibilities does the idea generator agent's system message list?","a":"<p>It generates innovative campaign ideas for the topic, suggests storylines, provides a brief outline for each idea, and thinks creatively to produce a variety of concepts.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0051","card":"q-autogen-011-agents","sec":"autogen-s010","q":"What does the script writer agent develop?","a":"<p>Full scripts from selected ideas. They include dialog, scene descriptions and camera directions, and must be engaging and professional.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0052","card":"q-autogen-011-agents","sec":"autogen-s010","q":"What does the script reviewer agent check?","a":"<p>It analyzes completed scripts and gives detailed feedback. It evaluates coherence, assesses engagement level, checks alignment with the campaign topic, and suggests improvements.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0053","card":"q-autogen-012-tasks-the-chat-queue","sec":"autogen-s011","q":"In the AutoGen sequential-chat research assistant, what does the task list for the research assistant look like?","a":"<p>A <code>chats</code> list with one dict per task. Task 1 is Manager to Idea Generator:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>chats = [\n    {\n        &quot;sender&quot;: manager_proxy,\n        &quot;recipient&quot;: idea_generator,\n        &quot;summary_method&quot;: &quot;reflection_with_llm&quot;,\n        &quot;max_turns&quot;: 2,\n        &quot;clear_history&quot;: True\n    },\n]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0054","card":"q-autogen-012-tasks-the-chat-queue","sec":"autogen-s011","q":"Why is <code>clear_history</code> <code>True</code> in the first task and <code>False</code> in the later ones?","a":"<p>The first task is independent and starts fresh. The later tasks carry context from the previous chats.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0055","card":"q-autogen-012-tasks-the-chat-queue","sec":"autogen-s011","q":"What is the final task in the research assistant chat queue?","a":"<p>Manager to Manager, a final decision on the script and any necessary revisions. It uses <code>max_turns</code> 1 and <code>clear_history</code> <code>False</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0056","card":"q-autogen-012-tasks-the-chat-queue","sec":"autogen-s011","q":"Which <code>max_turns</code> values do the research assistant tasks use?","a":"<p>The first three tasks use 2, so each allows iterative refinement. The final decision task uses 1.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0057","card":"q-autogen-012-tasks-the-chat-queue","sec":"autogen-s011","q":"In the AutoGen sequential-chat research assistant, what does the Script Writer task message ask for?","a":"<p>A full script for the marketing video based on the selected idea. It must include dialog, scene descriptions and camera directions.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0058","card":"q-autogen-012-tasks-the-chat-queue","sec":"autogen-s011","q":"In the AutoGen sequential-chat research assistant, what does the Script Reviewer task message ask for?","a":"<p>A review of the script with detailed feedback on coherence, engagement and alignment with the campaign goals.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0059","card":"q-autogen-013-run-and-inspect","sec":"autogen-s012","q":"How do you run a list of sequential chats in AutoGen?","a":"<p>Import <code>initiate_chats</code> and pass the list:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from autogen import initiate_chats\n\nchat_results = initiate_chats(chats)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0060","card":"q-autogen-013-run-and-inspect","sec":"autogen-s012","q":"How do you print each chat's summary after <code>initiate_chats</code>?","a":"<p>Loop over the results and print <code>chat_result.summary</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>for i, chat_result in enumerate(chat_results):\n    print(f&quot;\\n=== Chat {i+1} Summary ===&quot;)\n    print(chat_result.summary)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0061","card":"q-autogen-013-run-and-inspect","sec":"autogen-s012","q":"How do you see the cost of each chat in sequential chats?","a":"<p>Read <code>chat_result.cost</code> for each result:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>for i, chat_result in enumerate(chat_results):\n    print(f&quot;Chat {i+1} Cost: ${chat_result.cost}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0062","card":"q-autogen-013-run-and-inspect","sec":"autogen-s012","q":"What does <code>chat_results</code> hold?","a":"<p>For each chat, its summary and cost.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0063","card":"q-autogen-013-run-and-inspect","sec":"autogen-s012","q":"How do you add a follow-up chat dynamically based on a result?","a":"<p>Check the first result's summary and append a chat dict:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>initial_result = chat_results[0]\nif &quot;needs_revision&quot; in initial_result.summary:\n    chats.append({\n        &quot;sender&quot;: manager,\n        &quot;recipient&quot;: idea_generator,\n        &quot;message&quot;: &quot;Revise based on feedback&quot;\n    })</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0064","card":"q-autogen-014-6-nested-chats-reflection-pattern","sec":"autogen-s013","q":"What is a nested chat in AutoGen?","a":"<p>A conversation inside a conversation. An agent consults other agents before replying. It models multi-step processes, quality control and hierarchical decisions.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0065","card":"q-autogen-014-6-nested-chats-reflection-pattern","sec":"autogen-s013","q":"What is the architecture of the nested-chat reflection pattern?","a":"<p>The Reviewer agent talks to the Writer. When the Writer replies, the reviewer runs <strong>inner chats</strong> with specialist reviewers. It then sends consolidated feedback back to the Writer. The inner chats are the reviewer's \"inner monologue\".</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0066","card":"q-autogen-014-6-nested-chats-reflection-pattern","sec":"autogen-s013","q":"Which agent class do the nested chat writer and reviewers use?","a":"<p><code>AssistantAgent</code>, an LLM assistant customized via its system message.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0067","card":"q-autogen-015-agents","sec":"autogen-s014","q":"In AutoGen's nested-chat example, how do you define the writer agent and its task?","a":"<p>The writer is an <code>AssistantAgent</code> whose system message makes it a professional content writer. The task is a blog post about GPUs:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>writer = AssistantAgent(\n    name=&quot;writer&quot;,\n    system_message=&quot;&quot;&quot;You are a professional content writer.\n    Your role is to create engaging, well-structured content\n    based on the given topic.&quot;&quot;&quot;,\n    llm_config=llm_config\n)\n\ntask = &quot;&quot;&quot;Write a concise but engaging blog post about GPUs.&quot;&quot;&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0068","card":"q-autogen-015-agents","sec":"autogen-s014","q":"How do you test the writer alone in the nested chat example?","a":"<p>Call <code>generate_reply</code> with the task as a user message:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>reply = writer.generate_reply(messages=[{&quot;content&quot;: task, &quot;role&quot;: &quot;user&quot;}])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0069","card":"q-autogen-015-agents","sec":"autogen-s014","q":"How do you define the reviewer in the nested chats example, and how does it stop?","a":"<p>It is an <code>AssistantAgent</code> that gives constructive feedback on writing quality, clarity and engagement. It ends when a message contains \"TERMINATE\":</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>is_termination_msg=lambda msg: &quot;TERMINATE&quot; in msg.get(&quot;content&quot;, &quot;&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0070","card":"q-autogen-015-agents","sec":"autogen-s014","q":"In AutoGen's nested-chat example, how does a simple (non-nested) reviewer and writer interaction start?","a":"<p>The reviewer starts the chat with the writer:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>reviewer.initiate_chat(\n    recipient=writer,\n    message=task,\n    summary_method=&quot;last_msg&quot;\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0071","card":"q-autogen-016-specialized-reviewers","sec":"autogen-s015","q":"Which specialized reviewers does the nested chat example define?","a":"<p>Four <code>AssistantAgent</code> reviewers:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><code>seo_reviewer</code></li>\n  <li><code>grammar_reviewer</code></li>\n  <li><code>ethics_reviewer</code></li>\n  <li><code>meta_reviewer</code></li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0072","card":"q-autogen-016-specialized-reviewers","sec":"autogen-s015","q":"In AutoGen's nested-chat review example, what does the SEO reviewer check?","a":"<p>Keyword optimization, search engine ranking potential, meta descriptions and readability for SEO.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0073","card":"q-autogen-016-specialized-reviewers","sec":"autogen-s015","q":"In AutoGen's nested-chat review example, what does the grammar reviewer check?","a":"<p>Grammatical errors, spelling mistakes, sentence structure, and clarity and conciseness.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0074","card":"q-autogen-016-specialized-reviewers","sec":"autogen-s015","q":"In AutoGen's nested-chat review example, what does the ethics reviewer check?","a":"<p>Ethical issues, bias or discrimination, factual accuracy and responsible messaging.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0075","card":"q-autogen-016-specialized-reviewers","sec":"autogen-s015","q":"In AutoGen's nested-chat review example, what does the meta reviewer do?","a":"<p>It is the lead reviewer. It aggregates feedback from all specialized reviewers and provides an overall assessment, priority recommendations and a final verdict.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0076","card":"q-autogen-017-reflection-message-function","sec":"autogen-s016","q":"What can the <code>message</code> field of a nested chat entry be besides a string?","a":"<p>A function <code>(recipient, messages, sender, config)</code> that builds the message.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0077","card":"q-autogen-017-reflection-message-function","sec":"autogen-s016","q":"In AutoGen's nested-chat review example, how do you write a reflection message function that passes the writer's draft to a reviewer?","a":"<p>Return a prompt that includes <code>messages[-1]</code>, the latest message (the writer's draft), so content is passed automatically:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def reflection_message(recipient, messages, sender, config):\n    return f&quot;Review the following content:\\n\\n{messages[-1][&#x27;content&#x27;]}&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0078","card":"q-autogen-018-review-chat-queue-and-registration","sec":"autogen-s017","q":"What does an entry in the nested review chat queue look like?","a":"<p>A dict with the recipient, a message (the reflection function), a summary method and prompt, and <code>max_turns</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>{   # SEO review\n    &quot;recipient&quot;: seo_reviewer,\n    &quot;message&quot;: reflection_message,\n    &quot;summary_method&quot;: &quot;reflection_with_llm&quot;,\n    &quot;summary_args&quot;: {&quot;summary_prompt&quot;: &quot;Summarize SEO feedback&quot;},\n    &quot;max_turns&quot;: 1\n},</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0079","card":"q-autogen-018-review-chat-queue-and-registration","sec":"autogen-s017","q":"In AutoGen's nested-chat review example, how is the meta review entry different from the other review entries?","a":"<p>Its message is a plain string instead of the reflection function: <code>\"Aggregate all feedback and provide final assessment\"</code>. It aggregates all feedback from the earlier reviews.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0080","card":"q-autogen-018-review-chat-queue-and-registration","sec":"autogen-s017","q":"Which <code>max_turns</code> do you use for nested reviews?","a":"<p>Use <code>1</code> for a single focused specialist review, and about 3 for back-and-forth.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0081","card":"q-autogen-019-review-chat-queue-and-registration","sec":"autogen-s017","q":"How do you register nested chats on an agent?","a":"<p>Call <code>register_nested_chats</code> with the queue and a trigger agent:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>reviewer.register_nested_chats(\n    chat_queue=review_chats,\n    trigger=writer\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0082","card":"q-autogen-019-review-chat-queue-and-registration","sec":"autogen-s017","q":"What do <code>chat_queue</code> and <code>trigger</code> mean in <code>register_nested_chats</code>?","a":"<p><code>chat_queue</code> is the list of nested chat configs, run <strong>in sequence</strong>. <code>trigger</code> is the agent whose messages activate the nested chats. Here, they run whenever <code>writer</code> sends a message.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0083","card":"q-autogen-019-review-chat-queue-and-registration","sec":"autogen-s017","q":"In AutoGen's nested-chat review example, what is the execution order of the nested review pattern?","a":"<p>Reviewer sends the task to Writer, Writer drafts, the nested chats run (SEO, Grammar, Ethics, Meta), Reviewer sends consolidated feedback, and Writer improves.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0084","card":"q-autogen-019-review-chat-queue-and-registration","sec":"autogen-s017","q":"How do you start the nested chat reflection run and read the result?","a":"<p>Start a chat from the reviewer to the writer, then print the summary:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>result = reviewer.initiate_chat(\n    recipient=writer,\n    message=task,\n    summary_method=&quot;last_msg&quot;\n)\nprint(result.summary)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0085","card":"q-autogen-019-review-chat-queue-and-registration","sec":"autogen-s017","q":"In AutoGen's nested-chat review example, which other tasks fit the nested review pattern?","a":"<p>Code review (security, performance and style reviewers plus a lead) and paper review (methodology, statistics and ethics reviewers plus an editor).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0086","card":"q-autogen-019-review-chat-queue-and-registration","sec":"autogen-s017","q":"In AutoGen's nested-chat review example, why pass content through the reflection function rather than hard-coding text?","a":"<p>The function receives the latest message, so the reviewer sees the writer's actual draft each time.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0087","card":"q-autogen-019-review-chat-queue-and-registration","sec":"autogen-s017","q":"How can nested chats use a conditional trigger?","a":"<p>Pass a function as <code>trigger</code> that checks the last message:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def conditional_trigger(messages):\n    last_msg = messages[-1][&#x27;content&#x27;]\n    return &quot;review needed&quot; in last_msg.lower()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0088","card":"q-autogen-019-review-chat-queue-and-registration","sec":"autogen-s017","q":"How can reviewers be selected dynamically by content in the nested chat variant?","a":"<p>A function builds the reviewer list from keywords in the content:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def select_reviewers(content):\n    reviewers = []\n    if &quot;technical&quot; in content:\n        reviewers.append(technical_reviewer)\n    if &quot;marketing&quot; in content:\n        reviewers.append(marketing_reviewer)\n    return reviewers</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0089","card":"q-autogen-020-7-tool-use-and-web-search","sec":"autogen-s018","q":"What are tools in AutoGen?","a":"<p>Python functions the LLM can invoke. They extend an LLM beyond text, for example calculations, web search and databases.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0090","card":"q-autogen-020-7-tool-use-and-web-search","sec":"autogen-s018","q":"What is the two-agent pattern for tool use?","a":"<p>The <strong>assistant</strong> (LLM) suggests which tool to call. The <strong>user proxy</strong> (no LLM) executes it.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0091","card":"q-autogen-020-7-tool-use-and-web-search","sec":"autogen-s018","q":"Why do you register a tool twice in AutoGen?","a":"<p>The assistant suggests the tool and the user proxy executes it. This separation is why registration happens with both <code>register_for_llm</code> and <code>register_for_execution</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0092","card":"q-autogen-021-calculator-tool","sec":"autogen-s019","q":"How do you write a tool function so the LLM understands its arguments?","a":"<p>Use <code>Annotated</code> to document each argument for the LLM, and <code>Literal</code> to restrict the operator to allowed values:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def calculator(\n    a: Annotated[int, &quot;First number&quot;],\n    b: Annotated[int, &quot;Second number&quot;],\n    operator: Annotated[Literal[&quot;+&quot;, &quot;-&quot;, &quot;*&quot;, &quot;/&quot;], &quot;Operation&quot;]\n) -&gt; int:</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0093","card":"q-autogen-021-calculator-tool","sec":"autogen-s019","q":"What does <code>Literal</code> do in the calculator tool's signature?","a":"<p>It restricts the operator to the allowed values <code>\"+\"</code>, <code>\"-\"</code>, <code>\"*\"</code> and <code>\"/\"</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0094","card":"q-autogen-021-calculator-tool","sec":"autogen-s019","q":"What does the calculator tool do when the operator is invalid?","a":"<p>It raises an error:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>raise ValueError(&quot;Invalid operator&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0095","card":"q-autogen-021-calculator-tool","sec":"autogen-s019","q":"How is division done in the calculator tool?","a":"<p>With integer division:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return a // b</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0096","card":"q-autogen-021-calculator-tool","sec":"autogen-s019","q":"How do you create the assistant and the user proxy for the calculator tool?","a":"<p>The assistant has an LLM config. The user proxy is the execution agent, so <code>llm_config=False</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>user_proxy = ConversableAgent(\n    name=&quot;user_proxy&quot;,\n    llm_config=False,        # execution agent: no LLM\n    is_termination_msg=lambda msg: &quot;terminate&quot; in msg.get(&quot;content&quot;, &quot;&quot;).lower(),\n    human_input_mode=&quot;NEVER&quot;\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0097","card":"q-autogen-022-registering-tools-two-methods","sec":"autogen-s020","q":"How do you register a tool with direct registration?","a":"<p>Two calls: one on the assistant for the LLM, one on the user proxy for execution:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>assistant.register_for_llm(\n    name=&quot;calculator&quot;,\n    description=&quot;Performs basic arithmetic operations&quot;,\n)(calculator)\n\nuser_proxy.register_for_execution(\n    name=&quot;calculator&quot;\n)(calculator)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0098","card":"q-autogen-022-registering-tools-two-methods","sec":"autogen-s020","q":"How do you register a tool with the <code>register_function</code> utility?","a":"<p>One call with the function, the caller and the executor:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>register_function(\n    calculator,\n    caller=assistant,\n    executor=user_proxy,\n    name=&quot;calculator&quot;,\n    description=&quot;Performs basic arithmetic operations&quot;\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0099","card":"q-autogen-022-registering-tools-two-methods","sec":"autogen-s020","q":"Direct registration vs <code>register_function</code>: how do they compare?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Aspect</th><th>Direct registration</th><th><code>register_function</code></th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Calls</td><td>2 separate</td><td>1</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Error proneness</td><td>Higher</td><td>Lower</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Best for</td><td>Advanced customization</td><td>Standard use</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0100","card":"q-autogen-022-registering-tools-two-methods","sec":"autogen-s020","q":"Which tool registration method is recommended?","a":"<p>The <code>register_function</code> utility. It takes one call and is less error-prone.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0101","card":"q-autogen-022-registering-tools-two-methods","sec":"autogen-s020","q":"How do you start the calculator chat, and what happens?","a":"<p>The user proxy starts the chat with a math question:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>user_proxy.initiate_chat(\n    assistant,\n    message=&quot;What is (5 + 3) * (10 - 2) / 4?&quot;\n)</code></pre></div>\n<p>The assistant breaks the expression into calculator calls, the proxy executes each, and the assistant aggregates the result: 16.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0102","card":"q-autogen-022-registering-tools-two-methods","sec":"autogen-s020","q":"How do you register multiple tools on one agent?","a":"<p>Call <code>register_function</code> once per tool:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>register_function(calculator, caller=assistant, executor=user_proxy, name=&quot;calculator&quot;, description=&quot;Math operations&quot;)\nregister_function(search_tool, caller=assistant, executor=user_proxy, name=&quot;search&quot;, description=&quot;Web search&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0103","card":"q-autogen-023-web-search-with-tavily","sec":"autogen-s021","q":"How do you install the packages for web search with Tavily in AutoGen?","a":"<p>Install <code>pyautogen</code> and <code>tavily-python</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>pip install pyautogen tavily-python</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0104","card":"q-autogen-023-web-search-with-tavily","sec":"autogen-s021","q":"How do you create the Tavily client and the search tool?","a":"<p>Create a <code>TavilyClient</code> with the key from <code>TAVILY_API_KEY</code> and wrap its search in a function:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>tavily_client = TavilyClient(api_key=os.getenv(&quot;TAVILY_API_KEY&quot;))\n\ndef search_tool(query: Annotated[str, &quot;Search query&quot;]) -&gt; str:\n    return tavily_client.search(query=query)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0105","card":"q-autogen-023-web-search-with-tavily","sec":"autogen-s021","q":"In AutoGen web search, how do you get a Tavily API key?","a":"<p>Sign up at tavily.com, create a key in the dashboard, and put it in <code>.env</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0106","card":"q-autogen-023-web-search-with-tavily","sec":"autogen-s021","q":"In AutoGen web search, what is ReAct?","a":"<p>Reasoning plus Acting. It is a prompt template that makes the LLM alternate Thought, Action and Observation until it has a final answer. It improves accuracy and transparency.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0107","card":"q-autogen-023-web-search-with-tavily","sec":"autogen-s021","q":"In AutoGen web search, what does the ReAct prompt template contain?","a":"<p>The question, then repeating Thought, Action, Action Input and Observation lines, ending with:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>Thought: I now know the final answer\nFinal Answer: The final answer to the original question</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0108","card":"q-autogen-023-web-search-with-tavily","sec":"autogen-s021","q":"In AutoGen web search, how do you fill the ReAct template with a question?","a":"<p>Format the template with the input:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def format_prompt(question: str) -&gt; str:\n    return react_prompt.format(input=question)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0109","card":"q-autogen-023-web-search-with-tavily","sec":"autogen-s021","q":"Why does the web search user proxy use <code>human_input_mode=\"ALWAYS\"</code>?","a":"<p>The human approves each web search.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>human_input_mode=&quot;ALWAYS&quot;,     # human approves each web search</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0110","card":"q-autogen-023-web-search-with-tavily","sec":"autogen-s021","q":"In AutoGen web search, how does the web search flow work for \"Who won the T20 Cricket World Cup in 2024?\"","a":"<p>The assistant decides it needs search. The proxy runs Tavily and returns JSON results. The assistant then answers (\"India won\").</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0111","card":"q-autogen-023-web-search-with-tavily","sec":"autogen-s021","q":"How do you register the Tavily search tool for the research assistant?","a":"<p>Use <code>register_function</code> with the research assistant as caller:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>register_function(\n    search_tool,\n    caller=research_assistant,\n    executor=user_proxy,\n    name=&quot;search_tool&quot;,\n    description=&quot;Searches the web for current information&quot;\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0112","card":"q-autogen-023-web-search-with-tavily","sec":"autogen-s021","q":"What do you check if an AutoGen tool is never called?","a":"<p>Write a clear description, register it with both caller and executor, and mention the tool in the system message.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0113","card":"q-autogen-023-web-search-with-tavily","sec":"autogen-s021","q":"What are the other tool-use gotchas in AutoGen?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Infinite loops: add a termination condition and max rounds or turns.</li>\n  <li>Set <code>human_input_mode</code> by tool risk.</li>\n  <li>Validate tool inputs.</li>\n  <li>Rate-limit external APIs.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0114","card":"q-autogen-023-web-search-with-tavily","sec":"autogen-s021","q":"How does tool chaining work, for example search result to calculator?","a":"<p>It happens as sequential tool calls.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0115","card":"q-autogen-024-8-coding-copilot-code-execution","sec":"autogen-s022","q":"What is the two-agent pattern for the coding copilot?","a":"<p>A <strong>code writer</strong> (LLM) writes code but does not execute it. A <strong>code executor</strong> (no LLM) runs the code and returns output or errors. Errors go back to the writer, which fixes the code until it succeeds, giving automatic iterative debugging.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0116","card":"q-autogen-025-executor-and-agents","sec":"autogen-s023","q":"How do you create a local command-line code executor in AutoGen?","a":"<p>Use <code>LocalCommandLineCodeExecutor</code> with a timeout and a work directory:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>executor = LocalCommandLineCodeExecutor(\n    timeout=10,          # max execution seconds\n    work_dir=&quot;coding&quot;    # code files and outputs land here\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0117","card":"q-autogen-025-executor-and-agents","sec":"autogen-s023","q":"What do <code>timeout</code> and <code>work_dir</code> do on the code executor?","a":"<p><code>timeout</code> is the maximum execution time in seconds. <code>work_dir</code> is the folder where code files and outputs land.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0118","card":"q-autogen-025-executor-and-agents","sec":"autogen-s023","q":"How do you configure the code executor agent?","a":"<p>No LLM, linked to the executor, with human approval:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>code_executor_agent = ConversableAgent(\n    name=&quot;code_executor_agent&quot;,\n    llm_config=False,                              # no text generation\n    code_execution_config={&quot;executor&quot;: executor},  # link to executor\n    human_input_mode=&quot;ALWAYS&quot;,                     # human approves before code runs\n    default_auto_reply=&quot;Continue. Please keep solving the task until done.&quot;\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0119","card":"q-autogen-025-executor-and-agents","sec":"autogen-s023","q":"How do you configure the code writer agent?","a":"<p>An <code>AssistantAgent</code> with an LLM that never executes code:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>code_writer_agent = AssistantAgent(\n    name=&quot;code_writer_agent&quot;,\n    llm_config=llm_config,\n    code_execution_config=False,    # writes, never executes\n    human_input_mode=&quot;NEVER&quot;\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0120","card":"q-autogen-025-executor-and-agents","sec":"autogen-s023","q":"How can you see the default system message of <code>AssistantAgent</code>?","a":"<p>Read <code>code_writer_agent.system_message</code>. It says: You are a helpful AI assistant. Solve tasks for coding and language skills.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>system_message = code_writer_agent.system_message\nprint(system_message)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0121","card":"q-autogen-026-running-a-task","sec":"autogen-s024","q":"In the AutoGen coding copilot, how do you start the stock-graph coding task?","a":"<p>The executor agent starts a chat with the writer:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>code_executor_agent.initiate_chat(\n    code_writer_agent,\n    message=instruction\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0122","card":"q-autogen-026-running-a-task","sec":"autogen-s024","q":"In the AutoGen coding copilot, what is the flow of a coding copilot run?","a":"<p>The executor sends the task. The writer produces Python (yfinance and matplotlib) in a markdown code block, saved as <code>.py</code>. The executor asks the human for approval and runs it in <code>work_dir</code>. The writer then confirms or debugs.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0123","card":"q-autogen-026-running-a-task","sec":"autogen-s024","q":"In the AutoGen coding copilot, what does the instruction for the NVDA and TSLA graph ask for?","a":"<p>A graph of YTD stock performance for NVDA and TSLA as of today's date. The code goes in a markdown code block. The output is saved as <code>ytd_stock_gains.png</code> in the coding directory.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0124","card":"q-autogen-026-running-a-task","sec":"autogen-s024","q":"In the AutoGen coding copilot, how do you display the saved plot image in a notebook?","a":"<p>Use <code>IPython.display.Image</code> with the path:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>image_path = os.path.join(&quot;coding&quot;, &quot;ytd_stock_gains.png&quot;)\nImage(filename=image_path)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0125","card":"q-autogen-027-custom-functions-reduce-hallucination-re","sec":"autogen-s025","q":"In the AutoGen coding copilot, why give the code executor custom functions?","a":"<p>They reduce hallucination and provide reusable logic. The writer calls your functions instead of writing code from scratch.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0126","card":"q-autogen-027-custom-functions-reduce-hallucination-re","sec":"autogen-s025","q":"In the AutoGen coding copilot, how do you make custom functions available inside the execution environment?","a":"<p>Pass them in <code>functions</code> when creating the executor:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>executor = LocalCommandLineCodeExecutor(\n    timeout=60,\n    work_dir=&quot;coding&quot;,\n    functions=[get_stock_prices, plot_stock_prices]\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0127","card":"q-autogen-027-custom-functions-reduce-hallucination-re","sec":"autogen-s025","q":"What does <code>format_functions_for_prompt</code> do?","a":"<p>It extracts function signatures and docstrings and appends them to the writer's system message, so the writer knows to call them.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from autogen.coding import format_functions_for_prompt</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0128","card":"q-autogen-027-custom-functions-reduce-hallucination-re","sec":"autogen-s025","q":"In the AutoGen coding copilot, how do you append the custom function descriptions to the code writer's system message?","a":"<p>Concatenate the base message with the formatted functions:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>updated_message = code_writer_system_message + &quot;\\n&quot; + format_functions_for_prompt(\n    executor.functions\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0129","card":"q-autogen-027-custom-functions-reduce-hallucination-re","sec":"autogen-s025","q":"What must you do with the executor agent after creating a new executor with custom functions?","a":"<p>Recreate it with the same config (<code>llm_config=False</code>, <code>code_execution_config={\"executor\": executor}</code>, <code>human_input_mode=\"ALWAYS\"</code>) so it links to the new executor.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0130","card":"q-autogen-027-custom-functions-reduce-hallucination-re","sec":"autogen-s025","q":"In the AutoGen coding copilot, what code does the writer produce when custom functions exist?","a":"<p>It calls the user functions instead of writing from scratch:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>nvda_data = get_stock_prices(&#x27;NVDA&#x27;, &#x27;2024-01-01&#x27;, &#x27;2024-12-31&#x27;)\nplot_stock_prices(nvda_data, &#x27;coding/stock_prices.png&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0131","card":"q-autogen-027-custom-functions-reduce-hallucination-re","sec":"autogen-s025","q":"In the AutoGen coding copilot, what are the six steps of the coding copilot workflow?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Agent</th><th>Action</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>1</td><td>Executor</td><td>Sends task to writer</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>2</td><td>Writer</td><td>Generates code (using custom functions if given)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>3</td><td>Writer</td><td>Saves code to <code>.py</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>4</td><td>Executor</td><td>Requests human approval</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>5</td><td>Executor</td><td>Runs code in isolated work dir</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>6</td><td>Writer</td><td>Confirms success or debugs</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0132","card":"q-autogen-027-custom-functions-reduce-hallucination-re","sec":"autogen-s025","q":"What are the safety rules for code execution in AutoGen?","a":"<p>Keep <code>human_input_mode=\"ALWAYS\"</code> on the executor and review code before execution. Set a sensible <code>timeout</code>. Use an isolated <code>work_dir</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0133","card":"q-autogen-027-custom-functions-reduce-hallucination-re","sec":"autogen-s025","q":"In the AutoGen coding copilot, what do you check if custom functions are ignored or code runs fail?","a":"<p>For ignored functions: they need docstrings and type hints, <code>format_functions_for_prompt</code> must be applied, and the functions must be passed to the executor. For failed runs: check the timeout, that the work dir exists, and that required libraries are installed.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0134","card":"q-autogen-028-9-teachable-agents-long-term-memory","sec":"autogen-s026","q":"In AutoGen, what problems do standard LLM assistants have with memory?","a":"<p>Memory is lost when the chat ends. In-context learning is not persistent. Context windows fill up. Users repeat instructions every session.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0135","card":"q-autogen-028-9-teachable-agents-long-term-memory","sec":"autogen-s026","q":"What is a teachable agent?","a":"<p>An agent that learns from user interaction and keeps <strong>memos</strong> in a <strong>vector database (ChromaDB)</strong> that survives restarts. A <code>Teachability</code> capability object is added to a <code>ConversableAgent</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0136","card":"q-autogen-028-9-teachable-agents-long-term-memory","sec":"autogen-s026","q":"What is the flow of a teachable agent?","a":"<p>Teach a fact, preference or skill. The memo is embedded and stored. A later query is vectorized and a similarity search retrieves relevant memos. The response uses them.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0137","card":"q-autogen-028-9-teachable-agents-long-term-memory","sec":"autogen-s026","q":"Which kinds of things can a teachable agent learn?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Learnable type</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Facts</td><td>\"My birthday is June 15\"</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Preferences</td><td>\"I prefer bullet point summaries\"</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Skills</td><td>\"Always validate input before processing\"</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0138","card":"q-autogen-028-9-teachable-agents-long-term-memory","sec":"autogen-s026","q":"Standard agent vs teachable agent?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Standard agent</th><th>Teachable agent</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Memory</td><td>Single session</td><td>Persistent</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Personalization</td><td>None</td><td>Grows over time</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Instruction repetition</td><td>Every session</td><td>One-time teaching</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Context</td><td>Limited window</td><td>Extended via DB</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0139","card":"q-autogen-028-9-teachable-agents-long-term-memory","sec":"autogen-s026","q":"How do you install AutoGen with teachability support?","a":"<p>Install with the teachable extra. It installs AutoGen, ChromaDB and teachability dependencies:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>pip install &quot;pyautogen[teachable]&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0140","card":"q-autogen-028-9-teachable-agents-long-term-memory","sec":"autogen-s026","q":"How do you create a teachable agent?","a":"<p>Create the <code>Teachability</code> object and add it to the agent:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>teachability = Teachability(\n    reset_db=False,                              # True: clear all memory; False: load existing\n    path_to_db_dir=&quot;./tmp/teachable_agent_db&quot;    # database location\n)\n\nteachability.add_to_agent(teachable_agent)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0141","card":"q-autogen-028-9-teachable-agents-long-term-memory","sec":"autogen-s026","q":"What do <code>reset_db</code> and <code>path_to_db_dir</code> do in <code>Teachability</code>?","a":"<p><code>reset_db=True</code> clears all memory. <code>reset_db=False</code> loads existing memory. <code>path_to_db_dir</code> is the database location.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0142","card":"q-autogen-028-9-teachable-agents-long-term-memory","sec":"autogen-s026","q":"How do you chat with a teachable agent interactively?","a":"<p>Use a <code>UserProxyAgent</code> with <code>human_input_mode=\"ALWAYS\"</code> and start the chat from the teachable agent:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>teachable_agent.initiate_chat(\n    user,\n    message=&quot;Hi, I am a teachable user assistant. What&#x27;s on your mind?&quot;\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0143","card":"q-autogen-029-9-teachable-agents-long-term-memory","sec":"autogen-s026","q":"How does memory persist across sessions with <code>Teachability</code>?","a":"<p>In session 1, use <code>reset_db=True</code> to start fresh and teach the agent. In session 2, use <code>reset_db=False</code>, which prints \"Loading memory from disk\". Then \"What's my name?\" gives \"Hello, Harshit! How can I assist you today?\"</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>teachability = Teachability(reset_db=False)  # prints &quot;Loading memory from disk&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0144","card":"q-autogen-029-9-teachable-agents-long-term-memory","sec":"autogen-s026","q":"How do you teach a teachable agent a preference?","a":"<p>State it explicitly, for example that you always like summaries to have three bullet points: Title, Key Ideas, Key Takeaways. A new session with <code>reset_db=False</code> applies it without being told again.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0145","card":"q-autogen-029-9-teachable-agents-long-term-memory","sec":"autogen-s026","q":"How do you teach a teachable agent a skill or method?","a":"<p>First run a reasoning task with a \"think step by step\" prompt. Then teach the procedure so it applies to later problems. The procedure has six steps: understand the problem, write down what you know, identify what you need to find, create a plan, execute the plan, verify the solution.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0146","card":"q-autogen-029-9-teachable-agents-long-term-memory","sec":"autogen-s026","q":"In AutoGen teachable agents, which equation task is used to teach a method?","a":"<p>\"Consider this equation: 5 + 3 * 2 - 1 = 10. Can you modify exactly one integer on the left-hand side such that the right-hand side becomes 80?\" followed by \"Let's think step by step.\"</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0147","card":"q-autogen-029-9-teachable-agents-long-term-memory","sec":"autogen-s026","q":"How do you keep separate memory for each user of a teachable agent?","a":"<p>Use one DB path per user:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>user1_teachability = Teachability(path_to_db_dir=&quot;./db/user1&quot;)\nuser2_teachability = Teachability(path_to_db_dir=&quot;./db/user2&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0148","card":"q-autogen-029-9-teachable-agents-long-term-memory","sec":"autogen-s026","q":"How can you build a teachable agent per user ID?","a":"<p>Make a function that creates the agent and uses a per-user DB path:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def get_teachable_agent(user_id):\n    agent = ConversableAgent(name=f&quot;agent_{user_id}&quot;, llm_config=llm_config)\n    teachability = Teachability(path_to_db_dir=f&quot;./db/{user_id}&quot;)\n    teachability.add_to_agent(agent)\n    return agent</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0149","card":"q-autogen-029-9-teachable-agents-long-term-memory","sec":"autogen-s026","q":"What does the teachable agent's database folder contain?","a":"<p>Illustratively, a vector database <code>chroma.sqlite3</code>, serialized memos <code>memos.pkl</code> and an <code>embeddings/</code> folder. Exact files vary by version.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0150","card":"q-autogen-029-9-teachable-agents-long-term-memory","sec":"autogen-s026","q":"What are the tips for teaching an agent well?","a":"<p>Use explicit phrasing (\"I always prefer…\", \"Remember that…\"), teach one concept at a time, and verify with follow-up questions.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0151","card":"q-autogen-029-9-teachable-agents-long-term-memory","sec":"autogen-s026","q":"What do you do if teachable agent memory is not loading or the DB is corrupt?","a":"<p>If memory does not load, check <code>reset_db=False</code>, the correct path, and look for \"Loading memory from disk\". If the DB is corrupt, delete the folder and restart with <code>reset_db=True</code>. Persistence is automatic after each conversation.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0152","card":"q-autogen-030-10-group-chat-and-speaker-policies","sec":"autogen-s027","q":"What is a group chat in AutoGen?","a":"<p>Many specialized agents collaborate on a complex task. A <strong>GroupChatManager</strong> (LLM-based) selects the next speaker and broadcasts each message to all agents.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0153","card":"q-autogen-030-10-group-chat-and-speaker-policies","sec":"autogen-s027","q":"What is the group chat project and who are the agents?","a":"<p>A virtual data-analysis company analysing Apple stock for the past month.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Agent</th><th>Type</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Admin</td><td><code>UserProxyAgent</code></td><td>Gives task and feedback, approves deliverables</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Planner</td><td><code>AssistantAgent</code></td><td>Outlines steps and strategy</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Engineer</td><td><code>AssistantAgent</code></td><td>Writes the code</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Executor</td><td><code>ConversableAgent</code></td><td>Runs code, reports results/errors</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Writer</td><td><code>AssistantAgent</code></td><td>Compiles final report, refines on feedback</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0154","card":"q-autogen-030-10-group-chat-and-speaker-policies","sec":"autogen-s027","q":"How do you define the admin agent in the group chat?","a":"<p>A <code>UserProxyAgent</code> representing the client, with no code execution and human input always:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>admin = UserProxyAgent(\n    name=&quot;admin&quot;,\n    system_message=&quot;User proxy representing the client&quot;,\n    code_execution_config=False,\n    human_input_mode=&quot;ALWAYS&quot;\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0155","card":"q-autogen-030-10-group-chat-and-speaker-policies","sec":"autogen-s027","q":"How do you define the executor agent in the group chat?","a":"<p>A <code>ConversableAgent</code> with no LLM that runs code in the <code>coding</code> folder without Docker:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>executor = ConversableAgent(\n    name=&quot;executor&quot;,\n    system_message=&quot;You execute code and report results.&quot;,\n    llm_config=False,\n    human_input_mode=&quot;NEVER&quot;,\n    code_execution_config={\n        &quot;work_dir&quot;: &quot;coding&quot;,\n        &quot;use_docker&quot;: False\n    }\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0156","card":"q-autogen-030-10-group-chat-and-speaker-policies","sec":"autogen-s027","q":"In AutoGen group chat, what are the system messages of the planner, engineer and writer?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Planner: \"You determine what information is needed and outline steps to complete the task.\"</li>\n  <li>Engineer: \"You write code to fetch and analyze stock data.\"</li>\n  <li>Writer: \"You compile final reports based on data analysis results and refine based on feedback.\"</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0157","card":"q-autogen-031-10-group-chat-and-speaker-policies","sec":"autogen-s027","q":"In AutoGen's data-analysis group chat, what task does the admin start the chat with?","a":"<p>Analyzing Apple stock prices for the past month. The admin sends it to the chat manager:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>task = &quot;&quot;&quot;\nAnalyze the daily closing prices of Apple stock for the past one month \nand create a brief report.\n&quot;&quot;&quot;\n\nadmin.initiate_chat(\n    chat_manager,\n    message=task\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0158","card":"q-autogen-031-10-group-chat-and-speaker-policies","sec":"autogen-s027","q":"How do you create a <code>GroupChat</code> and a manager?","a":"<p>Create the <code>GroupChat</code> with agents, messages and <code>max_round</code>, then wrap it in a <code>GroupChatManager</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>group_chat = GroupChat(\n    agents=[admin, planner, engineer, executor, writer],\n    messages=[],        # conversation history\n    max_round=10        # max speaker selections; prevents infinite loops\n)\n\nchat_manager = GroupChatManager(\n    groupchat=group_chat,\n    llm_config=llm_config   # the manager needs an LLM to pick speakers\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0159","card":"q-autogen-031-10-group-chat-and-speaker-policies","sec":"autogen-s027","q":"What does <code>max_round</code> do in <code>GroupChat</code>?","a":"<p>It is the maximum number of speaker selections. It prevents infinite loops.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0160","card":"q-autogen-031-10-group-chat-and-speaker-policies","sec":"autogen-s027","q":"Why does the <code>GroupChatManager</code> need an <code>llm_config</code>?","a":"<p>The manager needs an LLM to pick speakers.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0161","card":"q-autogen-031-10-group-chat-and-speaker-policies","sec":"autogen-s027","q":"How do you start the group chat?","a":"<p>The admin starts a chat with the manager:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>admin.initiate_chat(\n    chat_manager,\n    message=task\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0162","card":"q-autogen-031-10-group-chat-and-speaker-policies","sec":"autogen-s027","q":"What is the typical flow in the Apple stock group chat, and what did the report cover?","a":"<p>Admin, Manager, Planner (strategy), Engineer (fetch code), Executor (data), Planner, Engineer (analysis code), Executor, Writer, Admin. The report covered count, mean and std, volatility, 5-day moving average, trend and recommendations.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0163","card":"q-autogen-032-speaker-selection-policy","sec":"autogen-s028","q":"What does <code>allowed_or_disallowed_speaker_transitions</code> do?","a":"<p>It maps each agent to the agents it may hand off to.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0164","card":"q-autogen-032-speaker-selection-policy","sec":"autogen-s028","q":"In AutoGen group chat, how do you restrict which agents can speak after which?","a":"<p>Define a transitions dict and pass it with <code>speaker_transitions_type=\"allowed\"</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>allowed_transitions = {\n    admin: [planner, engineer, executor, writer],\n    engineer: [admin, executor],\n    writer: [admin, planner],\n    executor: [admin, planner, engineer],\n    planner: [admin, engineer, writer]\n}\n\ngroup_chat = GroupChat(\n    agents=[admin, planner, engineer, executor, writer],\n    messages=[],\n    max_round=10,\n    allowed_or_disallowed_speaker_transitions=allowed_transitions,\n    speaker_transitions_type=&quot;allowed&quot;\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0165","card":"q-autogen-032-speaker-selection-policy","sec":"autogen-s028","q":"What are the two values of <code>speaker_transitions_type</code>?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th><code>speaker_transitions_type</code></th><th>Dictionary means</th><th>Use</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>\"allowed\"</code></td><td>Only these transitions are permitted</td><td>Strict, clear pathways</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>\"disallowed\"</code></td><td>These transitions are forbidden</td><td>Flexibility with guardrails</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0166","card":"q-autogen-032-speaker-selection-policy","sec":"autogen-s028","q":"In AutoGen group chat, how do you forbid the engineer and executor from talking directly to the writer?","a":"<p>Use a disallowed transitions dict:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>disallowed_transitions = {\n    engineer: [writer],   # engineer cannot talk directly to writer\n    executor: [writer]    # executor cannot talk directly to writer\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0167","card":"q-autogen-032-speaker-selection-policy","sec":"autogen-s028","q":"In AutoGen group chat, how do you build a hierarchical structure with speaker transitions?","a":"<p>Allow a CEO to talk to managers, managers to talk to their workers and back to the CEO, and workers only to their manager:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>allowed_transitions = {\n    ceo: [manager1, manager2],\n    manager1: [worker1, worker2, ceo],\n    manager2: [worker3, worker4, ceo],\n    worker1: [manager1],\n    worker2: [manager1]\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0168","card":"q-autogen-032-speaker-selection-policy","sec":"autogen-s028","q":"In AutoGen group chat, why use speaker transition policies?","a":"<p>They give structured communication and logical information flow, mirror org hierarchies, cut wasted turns (lower token cost), and force review checkpoints.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0169","card":"q-autogen-032-speaker-selection-policy","sec":"autogen-s028","q":"What are the group chat gotchas and fixes?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Loops: set <code>max_round</code>, check circular transitions, add termination.</li>\n  <li>Wrong agent speaking: check the policy dictionary, give the manager an LLM config, and make sure agent names and objects match the policy keys.</li>\n  <li>Poor collaboration: sharpen system messages, adjust transitions, add intermediate agents, raise <code>max_round</code>.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0170","card":"q-autogen-032-speaker-selection-policy","sec":"autogen-s028","q":"What are the best practices for agent roles in a group chat?","a":"<p>Give each agent one focused role with no overlapping responsibilities, and test agents individually first.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0171","card":"q-autogen-033-11-pattern-comparison-and-troubleshootin","sec":"autogen-s029","q":"Sequential chats vs nested chats vs group chat in AutoGen?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Aspect</th><th>Sequential chats</th><th>Nested chats</th><th>Group chat</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>API</td><td><code>initiate_chats(chats)</code></td><td><code>register_nested_chats(chat_queue, trigger)</code></td><td><code>GroupChat</code> + <code>GroupChatManager</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Flow</td><td>Fixed, predefined order; summaries carried forward</td><td>Inner consultations triggered by an agent's message</td><td>Dynamic, manager (LLM) picks next speaker</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Flexibility</td><td>Low</td><td>Medium</td><td>High (can be restricted with speaker policies)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Setup</td><td>Simplest</td><td>Moderate</td><td>Highest</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Best for</td><td>Linear workflows where each step needs the last</td><td>Review/quality-control loops, hierarchical decisions</td><td>Complex, unpredictable tasks</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0172","card":"q-autogen-033-11-pattern-comparison-and-troubleshootin","sec":"autogen-s029","q":"Which agent pairing do you use for tool use, code execution and persistent memory?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Agent pairing</th><th>When</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Assistant (suggests) + UserProxy (executes)</td><td>Tool use</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Writer (LLM) + Executor (no LLM)</td><td>Code generation and execution</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Agent + <code>Teachability</code></td><td>Persistent memory across sessions</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0173","card":"q-autogen-033-11-pattern-comparison-and-troubleshootin","sec":"autogen-s029","q":"What are the common AutoGen failure modes and fixes?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Infinite loops: add termination, <code>max_turns</code>, <code>max_round</code>, timeouts.</li>\n  <li>Tool never called: check description and registration.</li>\n  <li>Wrong speaker in group chat: check the policy dict and the manager LLM.</li>\n  <li>API key errors: check <code>.env</code> and <code>load_dotenv()</code>.</li>\n  <li>Memory not loading: check <code>reset_db</code> and the path.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0174","card":"q-autogen-033-11-pattern-comparison-and-troubleshootin","sec":"autogen-s029","q":"Which related frameworks should you know in interviews about AutoGen?","a":"<p>LangChain (LLM apps), CrewAI (role-based agents), LangGraph (stateful workflows) and Semantic Kernel (enterprise).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0175","card":"q-autogen-034-12-production-testing-projects-and-caree","sec":"autogen-s030","q":"How do you cut token use in AutoGen?","a":"<p>Use concise system messages and cap output length:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>llm_config = {&quot;max_tokens&quot;: 500, &quot;temperature&quot;: 0.7}</code></pre></div>\n<p>Other levers: cache API responses, reuse agent instances, memoize results, and track cost via <code>chat_result.cost</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0176","card":"q-autogen-034-12-production-testing-projects-and-caree","sec":"autogen-s030","q":"How do you unit test an AutoGen agent?","a":"<p>Create an agent with a test config, generate a reply and assert it exists:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def test_agent_response():\n    agent = ConversableAgent(name=&quot;test&quot;, llm_config=test_config)\n    response = agent.generate_reply(messages=[{&quot;role&quot;: &quot;user&quot;, &quot;content&quot;: &quot;Hello&quot;}])\n    assert response is not None</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0177","card":"q-autogen-034-12-production-testing-projects-and-caree","sec":"autogen-s030","q":"What should AutoGen integration tests cover?","a":"<p>Multi-agent conversations, tool execution, error handling and output format.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0178","card":"q-autogen-034-12-production-testing-projects-and-caree","sec":"autogen-s030","q":"What is the quick-start template for a two-agent AutoGen chat?","a":"<p>An assistant and a user proxy with <code>human_input_mode=\"TERMINATE\"</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>user = UserProxyAgent(name=&quot;user&quot;, human_input_mode=&quot;TERMINATE&quot;, code_execution_config=False)\n\nuser.initiate_chat(assistant, message=&quot;Your task here&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0179","card":"q-autogen-034-12-production-testing-projects-and-caree","sec":"autogen-s030","q":"What is on the AutoGen production checklist?","a":"<p>Env-var secrets, logging and monitoring, rate limits and quotas, cost monitoring, input validation and sanitization, human oversight for critical decisions, bias audits and disclosure of AI use.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0180","card":"q-autogen-034-12-production-testing-projects-and-caree","sec":"autogen-s030","q":"Where can you host AutoGen agents?","a":"<p>Local, AWS Lambda or Cloud Run, Docker with Kubernetes, or Azure Functions.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0181","card":"q-autogen-035-project-ideas-from-the-course","sec":"autogen-s031","q":"Which AutoGen project ideas fit each level?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Beginner: personal assistant with web search, code reviewer, research summarizer.</li>\n  <li>Intermediate: content pipeline (idea, writer, editor, SEO), data-analysis company (planner, engineer, executor, writer), customer support (classifier, KB search, responder, QA reviewer).</li>\n  <li>Advanced: software team with enforced hand-offs, research lab, trading system.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0182","card":"q-autogen-035-project-ideas-from-the-course","sec":"autogen-s031","q":"In the AutoGen project ideas, how do you set up the beginner personal assistant with web search?","a":"<p>Register the search tool with the assistant as caller and the user proxy as executor:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>assistant = ConversableAgent(name=&quot;assistant&quot;, llm_config=llm_config)\nuser_proxy = UserProxyAgent(name=&quot;user&quot;, human_input_mode=&quot;ALWAYS&quot;)\nregister_function(search_tool, caller=assistant, executor=user_proxy)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0183","card":"q-autogen-035-project-ideas-from-the-course","sec":"autogen-s031","q":"In the AutoGen project ideas, how do you enforce hand-offs in an advanced software team?","a":"<p>Use allowed speaker transitions between product manager, architect, developer, tester and devops:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>allowed_transitions = {\n    product_manager: [architect],\n    architect: [developer, product_manager],\n    developer: [tester, architect],\n    tester: [developer, devops],\n    devops: [product_manager]\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0184","card":"q-autogen-036-career-notes","sec":"autogen-s032","q":"Which skills does the AutoGen course name as in demand?","a":"<p>Python, LLM integration (OpenAI, Anthropic), agentic AI, and RAG patterns with tool use. Next-tier: LangChain, LangGraph, vector databases, MLOps. Complementary: Docker, cloud (AWS/GCP/Azure), CI/CD, and FastAPI for agent APIs.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0185","card":"q-autogen-036-career-notes","sec":"autogen-s032","q":"How does the course suggest structuring an AutoGen portfolio?","a":"<p>One folder per project with its own README, under a top-level README that showcases all projects:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Text</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>my-autogen-projects/\n├── README.md (showcase all projects)\n├── simple-assistant/</code></pre></div>\n<p>Projects include simple-assistant, research-assistant, coding-copilot and group-chat-company.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0186","card":"q-autogen-036-career-notes","sec":"autogen-s032","q":"In AutoGen, what should each portfolio project include?","a":"<p>A clear README with setup, demo video or GIFs, comments, <code>requirements.txt</code> and example outputs.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"autogen-f0187","card":"q-autogen-036-career-notes","sec":"autogen-s032","q":"Where are the official AutoGen docs and repository?","a":"<p>Docs at https://microsoft.github.io/autogen/ and code at https://github.com/microsoft/autogen.</p>","hand":true}];
